  <main>
    <h1>How the cohorts guide change</h1>
    <p class="strap">We combine brief teaching, measurable experiments, and community problem-solving so you leave with a set of small, testable habits — not a vague checklist.</p>

    <div class="sections">
      <section class="panel" data-reveal>
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Core pillars</h2>
        <div class="pillars">
          <div class="pillar">
            <strong>Anchor routines</strong>
            <div class="muted">Tiny daily rituals that stabilize biological rhythms — morning light, mealtime windows, evening wind-downs.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar">
            <strong>Signal & response</strong>
            <div class="muted">Learn simple ways to notice triggers and apply one short response — breath, brief movement, or a food swap.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar">
            <strong>Friendly experiments</strong>
            <div class="muted">Small tests with clear measures so you can tell what helps without overhauling everything at once.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel" data-reveal>
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Typical program flow</h2>
        <div class="process">
          <div class="step"><strong>1. Map</strong><div class="muted">Two examples of baseline tracking and intake conversation.</div></div>
